list.item:
The title part, its subparts joined by hyphens:
the title: for a council, three capitals for its place (C.MAI for Mainz); for a decretal, three for its pope (D.LEO), with Ps before a forged decretal's pope (D.PsCAL); for a collection or a penitential, its name or an abbreviation of it (COLL.Dach, COLL.400, P.HAL); UNK where the title isn't known;
the date, where wanted: four digits, the year (C.MAI-0813); the latest possible year, where the date is a range; 9999 where the date isn't known (EP.LupEuf-9999);
a further identifier, where needed: a decretal's number in Jaffé's register, in Kaltenbrunner's numbering (D.LEO-0447-414); a version, -v and a name (C.NIC-0325-vDIO1, Nicaea in the first Dionysiana; D.LEO-0446-410-v1).

sch:rule.sch:assert:
The document's code
                  () begins with its category's prefix (, for the category
                  ).
